# tcrsift multi-allele canonical TCR constant-region AA sequences (#113).
#
# This file ships per-allele sequences for the three human TCR constant
# genes. The auto-detect logic in `_pick_best_allele` scores each
# candidate allele against the donor's contig translation past VDJ and
# picks the highest-scoring match per clonotype. The chosen allele is
# recorded in `{chain}_allele_called`; alternatives that score above
# the configured agreement floor are listed in
# `{chain}_allele_alternatives` for the audit trail.
#
# Sources and provenance (NB: IMGT has more allele *numbers* than there
# are distinct PROTEIN forms — the 5 known human TRBC2 alleles collapse
# to only 2 distinct mature protein sequences, so this FASTA stores 2
# TRBC2 entries, not 5):
#
#   - All sequences are BARE MATURE protein (no synthetic J→C junction
#     prepend — that residue is read per-clone from contigs since #105).
#   - TRAC*01: UniProt P01848 / Ensembl ENST00000611116. The only known
#     human TRAC allele.
#   - TRBC1*01: UniProt P01850 / Ensembl ENST00000633705. The only
#     human TRBC1 protein form with an accessible authoritative
#     reference. IMGT lists TRBC1*02 but the only *02 protein-level
#     references found are non-human (gorilla / ferret / orangutan);
#     not packaged here.
#   - TRBC2*01-protein: NCBI AAA60662. **The most common TRBC2 protein
#     form in human populations.** Encoded by IMGT alleles *01, *02,
#     and *04 — the nucleotide variants among these three are
#     synonymous, all coding for the same mature protein. Pre-2.3
#     versions shipped only the *03-protein form (the Ensembl/UniProt
#     canonical entry) which silently stomped donor-truth E at position
#     9 for the ~99% of donors carrying this allele; see #113 audit.
#   - TRBC2*03-protein: UniProt A0A5B9 / Ensembl ENST00000466254. The
#     minor human TRBC2 protein form. K at mature position 9 — the
#     auto-detect picks this when the donor's contig codes for K.
#   - TRBC2*05-protein: not packaged — protein sequence not findable
#     in public databases without IMGT access. Users carrying *05
#     donors should add the entry manually.
#
# To regenerate this file:
#   python -m tcrsift._regen_canonical_constants --alleles
#
# To extend with additional alleles (e.g. TRBC2*02 / *04 / *05, or
# TRBC1*02), append a new FASTA entry with the convention
# `>{GENE}*{NN}|provenance|notes` — the loader keys on `{GENE}*{NN}`.
# The allele picker will scan it automatically.

